**Known README inaccuracies — do not replicate in Python docs, note as
Ruby-side issues.** The README's options table and prose describe a
smaller/different surface than the actual `Boukensha.run` signature:

- README claims `backend:` accepts only `:anthropic` or `:ollama` ("`|
  `backend:` | `:anthropic` | `:anthropic` or `:ollama` |"); the real
  signature's `case backend` branches on all five:
  `:anthropic`/`:openai`/`:gemini`/`:ollama`/`:ollama_cloud`, raising
  `ArgumentError` for anything else.
- README documents a `token_budget:` option (default `8192`) and a
  `max_tokens:` option (default `1024`); **neither exists** in the real
  `def self.run(...)` signature — the real per-reply cap parameter is named
  `max_output_tokens:` (no default shown in the signature itself; falls
  back to `task_class.max_output_tokens(task_settings)`), and there is no
  context/token-budget parameter of any kind anywhere in this step's code.
  This is the same category of README-vs-code drift flagged in prior
  plans (e.g. `01_struct_skeleton`'s `token_budget` note, `04_api_client`'s
  stale-backends-table note) — recommend the Python README document the
  *actual* signature (five backends, `max_output_tokens:`, no
  `token_budget:`) rather than mirroring the Ruby README's inaccuracies.

**Known dead code, still dead.** `LoopError` (re-added to `errors.rb` this
step) is not raised anywhere in `07_the_run_dsl` either — same status as
